## What this predicate means

**A `applies-in` B** — scoping typed-edge.  Says "memorial A is especially relevant in the context of memorial B" — letting guidance / rules declare scope-applicability without becoming context-specific artifacts themselves.  Widened in v0.8.0 to admit rules as domain (per `decisions/rules_as_first_class_type_2026_05_11.md` D4 lattice-with-lifting scope + D10 typed-edge introspection graph) and contexts as range (rule applies in context).  Combined with `inherits-from:` lattice edges, supports Cyc-style transitive applicability — a rule applying in context P also applies in any sub-context that inherits-from P.

