## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Asymmetric** — A applies-in B doesn't imply B applies-in A (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — no memorial applies in itself (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)
- **NOT transitive** (BUT — see Cyc-style transitive applicability via inherits-from below)

## When to use applies-in

Use `applies-in` for:

- Guidance memorials declaring relevant library/reference scope
- Rule memorials declaring runtime context scope
- Pattern memorials declaring applicable engagement type

## Cyc-style transitive applicability

When the range memorial has an inheritance lattice (`inherits-from:` chain), applicability is INHERITED — if rule R applies-in context P, and context Q inherits-from P, then R is implicitly applicable in Q.  This is the **lattice-with-lifting** semantic from Cyc's microtheory pattern, ported to sandbar's `:dt/subclass-of` machinery + sandbar.db.entailment's rdfs9 entailment.

